1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Every system hides one quiet question.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Who, really, holds the gun?

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Behind most "decentralized" networks
stands a board with extra steps —

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
a foundation, a multisig,
a switch someone can flip.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,500
We built the opposite.
A protocol tied to the mast.

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:28,000
Like Ulysses — deaf, on purpose,
to its own future pleas.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
No owner. No board. No override.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Locke wrote that we join together
to preserve what is ours. Property.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
And with it, a life — and a private
inner world no power was meant to read.

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,500
Privacy was never a feature.
It is a penumbra —

11
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:53,000
a right the old constitutions assumed,
but never had to spell out. Until now.

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,500
So we write it into the one language
that does not drift.

13
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:03,000
Five hundred in 2026 is five hundred in 2500 —
a constant no politics can quietly invert.

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Postern sells no coin. It sells protection,
support, and integrity you can prove.

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Never trust. Always verify.

16
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,500
The base belongs to no one.
Its maker steps away.

17
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:22,000
What remains is mathematics —
open, and yours to run.

18
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Postern. Privacy and security,
sold the honest way.

19
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Freedom you do not have
to ask permission for.
